            <ArticleTitle>Asthma severity in children and the quality of life of their parents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.apnr.2011.01.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study examines the effect of asthma severity of children aged 7-17 years and sociodemographic characteristics on the caregiver's quality of life. For parents of asthmatic children, there was a negative correlation between overall asthma severity and quality-of-life score. Measuring parental quality of life enables the development of effective asthma programs.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Published by Elsevier Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
